    "body": "@domenic yeah and no, I don't want the browser to just change I want it to be forced into stopping this practice by the spec so all browsers, current and future are blocked from doing this. As this is currently implemented it directly conflicts with the Drag & Drop API, As a Developer If you trying to get a droppable area implemented the last thing you want is an error in your code before the droppable or in the way you implemented the droppable to send you or the user to the file URI. \r\n\r\nAs a user, you don't want to lose everything you filled out on a form because it said drop your file here then failed to handle it, I have had this happen to me and I can't remember what site it was but it was like a 4 stage form 1 step after the other.\r\n\r\nIt annoys users, it annoys developer who the hell ever wanted this feature. yeah, coz I wanna see the ASCII output of binary files or the browser to download a copy of a binary file I just selected from my machine to my machine.",
