    "updated_at": "2019-07-29T14:51:34Z",
    "body": "Hmm, well, changing the spec doesn't force browsers to do anything. Instead, we collaboratively develop the spec with the community, including browser implementers. See https://whatwg.org/working-mode#changes.\r\n\r\nSo the next step if you want to move this forward is for you to get multiple browser implementers to agree that:\r\n\r\n1. They want to make this change;\r\n2. They think the spec should constrain them from ever changing their mind\r\n\r\nHistorically we have left these sort of UI decisions up to individual browsers, and not mandated very many of them in the spec, so I think (2) will be particularly controversial, even if you make progress on (1). In particular for these sorts of UI decisions browsers usually make decisions based on user research and testing; while I can appreciate that you personally find this feature annoying, it's quite possible that there are large portions of their population that depend on that workflow.\r\n\r\nBut you can't know until you ask!",
